{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.BuchbergerPBW.s_poly_decomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.BuchbergerPBW.s_poly_decomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgOps"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.BuchbergerPBW.s_poly_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.BuchbergerPBW.s_poly_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/BuchbergerPBW/s_poly_decomposition.lean#L57-L100","doc":"**S-polynomial decomposition — base (two-rule) case.**\n\nThe two rules `f₁, f₂` share a leading monomial `α` with unit\nleading coefficients `a₁, a₂`; the combination `c₁f₁ + c₂f₂` cancels\nat `α` (`c₁a₁ + c₂a₂ = 0`). Then the combination is a scalar multiple\nof the S-polynomial (witness `d = c₁·a₁`), which is the $n=2$ head of\nthe manuscript's telescoping sum.\n\nThe conclusion is a **concrete `AlgElement` equation** — the real\ncontent the former `holds : Prop` lacked. A complete proof needs\ncoefficient extensionality for `AlgElement` (a raw data structure;\nsee `AlgOps.lean` §6); supplying that ext principle is the remaining\nmanuscript step. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:ugb-s-poly-decomposition","label":"prop:ugb-s-poly-decomposition","md":"unital-groebner-bases/buchberger-and-pbw/ugb-s-polynomial-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.BuchbergerPBW.sPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.BuchbergerPBW.sPoly","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/BuchbergerPBW/s_poly_decomposition.lean#L50-L55","doc":"The **S-polynomial** about two rules with unit leading coefficients\n`a₁, a₂`: `S(f₁,f₂) = a₁⁻¹·f₁ − a₂⁻¹·f₂`, built from the concrete\n`AlgElement` scalar-multiplication and subtraction (`AlgOps.lean`).\nA real construction, not an axiom. ","signatureChunk":0}]}